      "writtenOn": "2024-12-10T17:05:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "They seem ballpark-correct. In the ~50GB/sec range, although it probably varies a lot by machine.\n\nI think the best way to measure memory bandwidth would be to stride through memory in cache-line strides. Something like\n\nb :\u003d make([]byte, ...)\nvar sum byte\nfor i :\u003d 0; i \u003c len(b); i +\u003d 64 { sum +\u003d b[i] }\nsink \u003d sum\n\nThen you\u0027re doing ~no work per byte pulled in from whatever cache level `b` fits into.",
      "parentUuid": "017e18db_ffb93b3e",
      "revId": "3795dd5dec4955bf3db7e5840e43f66629f73fea",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705"
